[["wrb.fr",null,"[null,[\"c_2a762740804afa93\",\"r_aa10eb24624cddf4\"],null,null,[[\"rc_2a88edd4384c309e\",[\"To see what `luuquangvu` is referencing and why there is a discrepancy between his claim (120s / 450s) and the 20s watchdog behavior, we can fetch the source of `client.py` directly from GitHub using the `gh` CLI. \\n\\nRun this command in your terminal:\\n\\n```bash\\ngh api repos/HanaokaYuzu/Gemini-API/contents/src/gemini_webapi/client.py --jq .content | base64 -d | grep -n -C 5 \\\"watchdog\\\"\\n```\\n\\nor search for the timeouts defined on `GeminiClient`:\\n\\n```bash\\ngh api repos/HanaokaYuzu/Gemini-API/contents/src/gemini_webapi/client.py --jq .content | base64 -d | grep -n -C 5 \\\"timeout\\\"\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### What `luuquangvu` is Arguing vs. What You Are Experiencing\\n\\n1. **Where `luuquangvu` is coming from:**\\n   - He believes the library defaults to:\\n     - `watchdog_timeout \\u003d 120` seconds\\n     - `timeout \\u003d 450` seconds\\n   - Seeing `[Watchdog] Socket idle for 20s` in your issue led him to believe your environment was configured with a non-default 20-second threshold.\\n   - Because 120 seconds is generally longer than the 20–40 seconds Gemini takes to output the first reasoning chunk, his reaction is: *\\\"With the default 120s timeout, reasoning stalls shouldn't trigger the watchdog.\\\"*\\n\\n2. **Why 20 Seconds Appears Without Any Custom Configuration:**\\n   If you did not pass custom timeout arguments, the 20-second threshold typically comes from one of two places in the code:\\n   - **Hardcoded Internal HeartbeatThe reason for the\"],null,null,null,null,null,null,[1],\"en\",null,null,[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,[[[],\"Searched the web\",\"Google Search\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg\",[],\"Searched the web\",\"\",[[\"https://t1.gst